WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:04.120
 RStudio Cloud  

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:07.840
 currently supports three project types, 
  RStudio projects, 

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:12.280
 projects from a Git repository, 
  and our newest feature, Jupyter Projects. 

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:16.240
 This means that as instructors, 
  we have a good deal of flexibility 

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:18.840
 over the coding environment 
  we create for our learners, 

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.960
 and that we can teach using 
  both R and Python 

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.000
 within the same cloud-based environment. 

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:27.960
 We can access each of these project  

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.800
 types by clicking on the arrow 
  in the right hand side of the new projects 

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:37.440
 button. When we select RStudio project, 
  we're taken to a new untitled project 

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:41.440
 within the RStudio IDE.  

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:53.280
 When we select Jupyter Project 
  we're taken to a new untitled project 

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:54.120
 that gives us all  

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:57.560
 of the same functionality 
  we expect from within a Jupyter Project, 

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:01.160
 including the ability to upload files, 
  as well as create 

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:04.360
 new Python notebooks 
  using specific versions of Python. 

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:19.200
 We can also clone a new RStudio 

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:23.680
 or Jupyter project from a git 
  repository. For RStudio projects 

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:27.200
 we simply provide the URL of 
  the corresponding git repository, 

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:31.040
 while for Jupyter we can accomplish this 
  by cloning our repository 

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:34.880
 from a new terminal within a Jupyter 
  project on RStudio Cloud. 

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:39.240
 RStudio support for Jupyter 
  projects is exciting, 

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:42.640
 although at the time of this recording, 
  the feature is still in beta. 

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:46.120
 We would love to hear your feedback, 
  and you can always reach out to us 

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:50.440
 on the community 
  forums at community.rstudio.com/c/rstudio-cloud

